1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,703
Welcome! This video teaches you Spirits of the Wild, a quick two player game of collecting colorful stones.

2
00:00:06,928 --> 00:00:18,020
Legend says that five forest animals rose to the stars and came back as spirits. Bring them beautiful stones and they will reward you. But watch out for the jealous Coyote, who loves to get in the way.

3
00:00:18,245 --> 00:00:27,920
Your goal is simple. Use your action cards to get stones, give them to the five animals on your board, and score the most points. Each animal wants a different pattern of colors.

4
00:00:28,145 --> 00:00:39,562
In the box you will find a bowl, a cloth bag, the Coyote pawn, two player boards, twelve action cards, six Spirit Power cards, and fifty six stones: eight in each of seven colors.

5
00:00:39,787 --> 00:00:51,866
The eight clear stones are Spirit Stones. They can only go on an animal's bonus space, where they double that animal's points. And they are the game clock: when the fifth Spirit Stone has left the bag, the game ends.

6
00:00:52,091 --> 00:00:56,496
Setup. Put the bowl between the two players, and set the Coyote to the side.

7
00:00:56,721 --> 00:01:07,313
Put all the stones into the bag and shake it. Then draw four stones into the bowl. If you draw a clear Spirit Stone, put it back and draw a new one, so the bowl starts with four colored stones.

8
00:01:07,538 --> 00:01:13,023
Each player takes a player board and a set of six action cards, laid out face up in front of the board.

9
00:01:13,248 --> 00:01:20,683
Shuffle the six Spirit Power cards and make two face-up piles of three cards. Only the top card of each pile can be chosen.

10
00:01:20,908 --> 00:01:31,953
Finally, choose a start player. To balance the first move, the start player turns their Take Two Stones card face down. They can't use it until they recover their cards. Now you are ready to play!
